# conflicts of interest: roles without access, and the files they leave out of rounds
board = Board
auditor = Audit committee
staff = Staff
coi.no.wiki.account = no wiki account, can''t be checked for conflicts of interest
coi.files = Conflicts of interest
coi.exclude = Leave out conflicts of interest
coi.count = {0} of the contest''s files are conflicts of interest (by its members or root users).
coi.count.round = {0} of this round''s files are conflicts of interest, {1} of the contest''s (by its members or root users).
coi.exclude.edit = Ticked on a round that didn''t leave them out, saving disqualifies them, keeping their votes aside (only while the round is stopped; on an open round only later distributions leave them out). Later matches are disqualified on the round''s conflicts page. Unticked, later distributions may add them.
coi.exclude.confirm = Disqualify the {0} files that are conflicts of interest in this round? Their votes are kept aside, and come back if a file is requalified.
coi.without.author = {0} of the contest''s files have no author.
coi.remove.distributing = Round {0}: its images are being distributed. Leave out conflicts of interest once it has finished.
coi.disqualified = Round {1}: {0} files disqualified as conflicts of interest; their votes are kept.
coi.disqualify.open = Round {0} is open to its jurors: its later distributions leave its {1} conflicts of interest out. To disqualify them, stop the round, then use its conflicts page:
coi.disqualify.frozen = Round {0}: a next round''s distribution is reading its votes. Try again once it has finished.
coi.action.open = Round {0} is open to its jurors: stop it first to disqualify or requalify files.
coi.requalified = Round {1}: {0} files requalified, with their votes.
coi.none.selected = No file selected.
coi.requalify.reason.missing = Choose why the files are requalified.
coi.round.link = Conflicts of interest of this round
coi.round.title = Conflicts of interest
coi.round.title.of = Conflicts of interest of round {0} {1}
coi.round.help = The round''s files whose author is one of the contest''s members in a role with a conflict of interest, or a root user. Disqualifying a file takes it out of the jurors'' lists and the results and keeps its votes; requalifying it brings them back. Both only while the round is stopped.
coi.role.help = Jurors, organizers and admins: their own photos (by their wiki account) are conflicts of interest too. Board, Audit committee and Staff give no access; they only mark the person''s photos as conflicts of interest.
coi.round.matches = Conflicts of interest in the round
coi.round.matches.none = None of the round''s files is a conflict of interest now.
coi.round.disqualified = Disqualified files
coi.round.disqualified.none = No file of this round is disqualified.
coi.round.back = Back to the round
coi.select = Select
coi.file = File
coi.person = Whose
coi.reason = Reason
coi.disqualified.at = Disqualified on
coi.match.now = Now
coi.match.ended = No longer a conflict of interest
coi.match.still = Still a conflict of interest: {0}
coi.disqualify = Disqualify the selected files
coi.disqualify.help = Their votes are kept aside; "Distribute new files" never adds them again. This doesn''t change the round''s "Leave out conflicts of interest": its later distributions leave out new conflicts only if that is ticked.
coi.requalify = Requalify the selected files
coi.requalify.help = Their votes come back as they were. A file still a conflict of interest is offered for disqualifying again.
coi.requalify.reason = Why
coi.requalify.reason.mistaken_match = A mistaken match
coi.requalify.reason.conflict_ended = The conflict has ended
coi.code.coi = Conflict of interest
